{"nodes": [{"id": "docs_src_content_docs_cluster_downing_strategies_downingprovider", "label": "DowningProvider", "file_type": "concept", "rationale": "Re-run on every cluster event with the current view, returning the addresses to forcibly down; an empty set means 'no decision yet - wait'. Without a provider the cluster sees unreachable members forever and operators must call cluster.down() by hand.", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/cluster/downing-strategies.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_cluster_downing_strategies_keepmajority", "label": "KeepMajority", "file_type": "concept", "rationale": "The most general default with no external dependencies and predictable behaviour for odd N; it cannot handle an exact N/2 split (both sides down) and is blind to physical topology.", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/cluster/downing-strategies.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_cluster_downing_strategies_keepoldest", "label": "KeepOldest", "file_type": "concept", "rationale": "Despite the name it does not track join order - 'oldest' is the lowest host:port, the same rule Cluster.leader() uses - so a node that joined a minute ago beats one up for a week. Pick it for a deterministic agreed tiebreaker and pin the surviving node's address; downIfAlone prevents a one-node winner after a total split.", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/cluster/downing-strategies.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_cluster_downing_strategies_keepreferee", "label": "KeepReferee", "file_type": "concept", "rationale": "The most predictable strategy and works for even-sized clusters, but it cannot decide if the referee itself disappears - hence downAllIfBelowQuorum. Useful for two-DC clusters with a neutral tie-breaker.", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/cluster/downing-strategies.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_cluster_downing_strategies_staticquorum", "label": "StaticQuorum", "file_type": "concept", "rationale": "Stricter than majority and errs toward fail-stop, but does not recover automatically; the quorum is checked at every membership change including the initial join, so a quorum above the starting size downs the cluster on startup.", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/cluster/downing-strategies.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_cluster_downing_strategies_leasemajority", "label": "LeaseMajority", "file_type": "concept", "rationale": "Majority plus a coordination lease - belt and braces for unpredictable networks - but it does not help if the lease provider itself is partitioned away.", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/cluster/downing-strategies.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_cluster_downing_strategies_abandoned_acquire", "label": "Abandoned lease acquire handling", "file_type": "rationale", "rationale": "The interesting case is 'the lease said nothing': every attempt carries an epoch so a late true cannot write a decision after the fact; a late win is released and no new attempt starts until it is, because overlapping attempts are how cleanup deletes a lease this side is claiming; and if the release fails the strategy enters fail-safe and decides nothing until the partition heals. The symptom of a bad lease provider is a cluster that waits, not one that splits.", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/cluster/downing-strategies.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_cluster_downing_strategies_clusterpartitionview", "label": "ClusterPartitionView", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/cluster/downing-strategies.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}], "edges": [{"source": "docs_src_content_docs_cluster_downing_strategies_keepmajority", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_cluster_downing_strategies_downingprovider", "relation": "implements", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/cluster/downing-strategies.mdx", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_src_content_docs_cluster_downing_strategies_keepoldest", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_cluster_downing_strategies_downingprovider", "relation": "implements", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/cluster/downing-strategies.mdx", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_src_content_docs_cluster_downing_strategies_keepreferee", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_cluster_downing_strategies_downingprovider", "relation": "implements", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/cluster/downing-strategies.mdx", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_src_content_docs_cluster_downing_strategies_staticquorum", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_cluster_downing_strategies_downingprovider", "relation": "implements", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/cluster/downing-strategies.mdx", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_src_content_docs_cluster_downing_strategies_leasemajority", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_cluster_downing_strategies_downingprovider", "relation": "implements", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/cluster/downing-strategies.mdx", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_src_content_docs_cluster_downing_strategies_leasemajority", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_cluster_downing_strategies_keepmajority", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/cluster/downing-strategies.mdx", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_src_content_docs_cluster_downing_strategies_downingprovider", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_cluster_downing_strategies_clusterpartitionview", "relation": "shares_data_with", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/cluster/downing-strategies.mdx", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_src_content_docs_cluster_downing_strategies_abandoned_acquire", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_cluster_downing_strategies_leasemajority", "relation": "rationale_for", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/cluster/downing-strategies.mdx", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_src_content_docs_cluster_downing_strategies_keepoldest", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_cluster_overview_leader", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/cluster/downing-strategies.mdx", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_src_content_docs_cluster_downing_strategies_downingprovider", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_cluster_failure_detector_failuredetector", "relation": "cites", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/cluster/downing-strategies.mdx", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_src_content_docs_cluster_downing_strategies_downingprovider", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_cluster_overview_cluster", "relation": "cites", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "